
-- The strategy pattern allows to obtain a set of algos
and encapsulate them in independent classes so that they can be
used interchangeably.

-- it separates the definition of algos from their usage allowing the algos
to vary independently of the client code.

-- payment systems

 interface --> implement classes --> class which uses stratergies -->main class
 pay --> concrete --> shopping cart --> main calling shopping


 when to use--

 when have multiple algos to chose from and want the flexibility to switch between then at
 runtime.

 -- payment, sorting

 -- Summary
  The strategy design pattern encapsulates algos in independent classes allowing them to be used
  interchangeably without modifying the client code.


